WEBVTT

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.640
Strike two!

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.380
The Hornets are up against a wall.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.590
Two outs, no runners on base, and Murdoch stands in the box.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.920
The Hornets' lineup has had several comebacks in the past,

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.690
but will they be able to create another miracle here?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.150
Strike out!

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.540
Game over!

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.420
Game over!

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.970
Four wins, two losses.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:36.170
The Anaheim Salmons have defeated the Indiana Hornets to take the Northern League title.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:42.470
They will be going on to play against the Texas Raiders in the World Series.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.720
We got close.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.780
Everyone played well, but we didn't have enough pitchers.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.700
It's our fault for not being out there.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.640
Next year, let's...

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.870
No, let's clear away this frustration even if it takes forever.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.160
We'll take the Hornets to the World Series with our own hands.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.500
Yeah.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.760
To the Future

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.760
To the Future

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.710
Morning, Shigeno!

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.830
It's Sophia!

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:21.880
Are you awake?

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.810
Goodness, is he still sleeping?

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.150
I told him to go to bed and get up early.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.070
How long do you plan to stay in—

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.740
Huh?

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.920
My, my...

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.080
Where did he go?

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.040
Geez...

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.460
You're unbelievable!

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.680
Haven't I told you before?

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.380
Do you know how unsafe it is to exercise right now?

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.780
Shut up.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.540
I do know!

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.140
Just...

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:03.260
I just couldn't stay put.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.120
I couldn't help my team when they needed me,

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.030
and I'm just spending my days doing nothing.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.860
I understand how you feel, but never do this again.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.270
If you keep it up, I can revoke your permission to return to Japan during the off season.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:26.180
Would you like to celebrate the new year in your small, lonely apartment?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.730
Are you serious?

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:30.790
Dead serious.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.270
The World Series came to an end.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:39.880
The Raiders beat the Salmons four games to three, and Junior definitely gets some of the credit.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.090
They became World Champions.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.890
On the other hand,

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.430
I was seeing doctors for follow-ups under the team's surveillance,

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:54.260
had my life and meals managed by Sophia,

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.580
and the only exercise I got was a two-hour walk in the park every morning and evening.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.580
A rather boring life, if you ask me.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.530
I'm finally free from that life.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.290
The yips and a circulation problem...

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.340
We somehow managed to be district champions,

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.100
but it wasn't exactly a smooth season.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.600
I still haven't reached their level.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.620
Just you wait...

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.970
I'll be a world champion next year.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:42.070
Huh?

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.120
Why'd you shower instead of just being grubby like usual?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.680
Who's grubby?

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.830
And what a thing to say for kid your age.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.370
Shigeno took a flight back here this morning.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:59.310
She got an email to go over and hang out if she has time, since he'll be home by eleven.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.860
Really, to hang out?

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.960
Great coffee.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:07.680
Maybe he really means "we need to talk."

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.980
What?!

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.660
With the rough season he had,

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.530
maybe he went and found a blue-eyed girl to give him some moral support.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.620
That's impossible!

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.360
That baseball fanatic would never show any interest in...

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.710
I'll come cook breakfast tomorrow at eight.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.260
Okay, thanks.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.700
He wouldn't... right?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.750
<b>Honda Family</b>

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.820
I wish you could have seen it too.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.340
Gibson and Junior had an amazing match.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.260
I was a bit jealous.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:01.360
I wish I could have had a showdown like that with you, Dad.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:04.900
Well, then...

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.190
I'll come back before I leave Japan.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.690
Give my regards to Mom.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.290
I'm home!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.210
Or wait...

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.850
What the heck?

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.110
I called and told them their cute son was coming back,

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.760
but they're not here to welcome me.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.390
Oh yeah, Shimizu's coming at eleven.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.930
I guess I'll take a quick shower.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:40.250
Taiga, you shouldn't tease her too much.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.860
But, who knows?

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:48.390
Maybe she'll find a Japanese man in his undies and a blonde in a towel,

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:51.740
making love at his house.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.950
Welcome back, Shigeno.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.080
Momoko took the kids and went out shopping.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.960
Wait, wh-why are you in my house?!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.570
No, in Japan?!

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.590
The management sent me.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:13.480
You're allowed to be here, but only under my watch.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:18.230
You're not exactly trustworthy when you tried to train immediately after the surgery.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:22.220
I already received permission from your parents.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.880
I'll be staying at your house while you're here.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.430
Impossible...

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:29.700
You better be freaking kidding me!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.740
Hurry up and get dressed!

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.770
And get out!

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:37.310
Why would I have to listen to you when I'm in—

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.160
Excuse me...

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:44.460
A Japanese man in his undies

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.930
and a blonde in a towel.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.810
H-Hey, Shimizu!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.280
This isn't what it looks like!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.490
Anyway, come on in!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:06.900
It's a misunderstanding!

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:07.900
Come back!

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.990
Hey, come back, Shimizu!

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.070
Unbelievable!

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.850
That must be the woman I heard over the phone.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:17.870
Watch out, Shimizu!

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.980
He really had a girlfriend overseas!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.760
<b>m 0 0 l 40 0 40 206 0 207
</b>

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.760
Stop!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.760
Stop!

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:31.420
What did I tell you?

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.350
Wh-Who...

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.630
Who is that woman?

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.110
I need an explanation!

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.520
You're being ridiculous.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:47.610
She's "security" that the team management placed on me.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:52.570
I apparently suck at managing my life, so she came all the way to Japan.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.200
And I just found that out.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.330
And we bumped into each other as I was going to take a shower.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.460
R-Really?

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.310
Of course, are you an idiot?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:10.970
Besides, I didn't have enough time over there to fall in love with another woman.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:15.790
Honda...

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.970
Mama, don't you think he's cold?

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.940
Hey, no pointing!

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.920
Why is he in his underwear?

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.900
Wait, don't look!

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.520
So that's Shigeno's girlfriend.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.700
So this is the famous Japanese sukiyaki.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.530
I've never had it before, but it's delicious!

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.510
Really?

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:39.950
That's great.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.250
There's plenty of meat, so have as much as you'd like.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.090
Yes, thank you very much.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:49.230
Sophia, your Japanese is very good.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.380
I studied it in America.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.960
Hey, miss, let's play a game later.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.150
Me too!

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.480
I want to play too!

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:57.260
Game?

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.850
Yes, okay!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.470
I'm done.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.770
Already?

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:03.230
Yeah.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:07.400
Our family reunion has been interrupted.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:12.070
I can't even relax when I come back to Japan.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.780
Hey, Goro!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.680
I'm sorry, he's so insensitive.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:21.700
Oh, it's fine.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:28.010
But are you sure I'm not a nuisance here?

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.940
No, we're actually very thankful to you.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:35.090
He's been pushing himself way too much.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.970
He tries to overcome anxiety and impatience with training,

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:40.940
so he needs the supervision.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.890
As a parent,

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.790
I'd say this is very welcome.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.110
Hello?

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.230
Hey, Shimizu?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.360
It's me.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.740
Do you have softball practice or something tomorrow?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.280
No, not really.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.560
Then do you want to go somewhere?

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.720
I just can't stand being in the house.

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.880
I never thought he'd take me out.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:19.800
Besides, I didn't have enough time over there to fall in love with another woman.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.170
I'm so happy there's nothing going on with that woman.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.660
Hey, sorry for being a little late.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.220
Hey, Hon—

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:29.390
Y-Yo...

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:35.250
Hey, why is she here?!

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.290
Sorry.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:39.360
I tried to lose her, but she's pretty good.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.240
So long as he doesn't try to stress his body, I won't butt in.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.180
Your presence alone ruins the experience.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.880
That was fun.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.820
Some people saw you when we were in a crowd.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.660
Saying you were Shigeno Goro.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.490
Oh, did they?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:25.030
In any case, I had absolutely zero fun.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.630
All thanks to her!

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:35.190
I couldn't do anything about her coming to Japan,

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.930
but I can't take any more.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.200
Look, I promise you that I won't do any training or baseball practice,

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.960
and I'll follow your manual about the meals,

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.100
so please go back to America.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.270
Please!

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:55.360
Fine.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:12:00.630
I can't give the okay myself, but I'll ask the management.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:01.750
Really?

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:05.780
However, we're not doing this to annoy you.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.950
We do this because you're the Hornets' ace candidate.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:17.720
We want to nurture you by understanding your personal life, family, and friends.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:22.550
By the way, are you two dating?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.870
Or just friends?

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.740
W-We're dating!

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:28.720
Can't you tell?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.090
Oh, really?

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.510
You don't hold hands or even touch each other much,

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:34.900
so I thought you were just friends.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.980
T-Touch...?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.400
Then are you two in a serious relationship, considering marriage?

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.950
Wh-What if we are?

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.190
That has nothing to do with you!

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:51.910
Shimizu Kaoru, second year of college?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.210
Y-Yes.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.580
From what I saw today, you're rather immature.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:00.500
Are you prepared to be the wife of a major leaguer?

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.720
If you can't think about marriage right now,

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:10.350
and you have your own dreams to pursue after you graduate,

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.680
I'd like you to break up with him as soon as possible.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:24.860
Nice pitch!

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:27.490
Good workout!

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:30.580
I have to say, you threw some really nice pitches.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.950
You're definitely next year's ace.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:35.150
Hey, Makiko...

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.250
What?

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.920
What's a woman's happiness?

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:40.980
Huh?

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.260
Who does she think she is?!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.800
She told you to break up?

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.710
Are you stupid?

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:48.450
That's none of her business!

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.360
Well, yeah...

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:52.060
That's enough!

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:56.980
Who I go out with or when I marry is none of your business!

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.010
It is my business!

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:02.570
Especially for a reckless player like you.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:06.690
If you have a family, you'll have that extra responsibility.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:11.510
You'll take care of yourself to play baseball even longer,

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:14.260
even if we don't keep an eye on you.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.680
Well, she does have a point.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.750
Really?

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:24.910
We've been in a long-distance relationship for a year,

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:28.680
but I can't think about marriage as a student,

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:35.710
so maybe it's better if he finds someone who can spend more time with him.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:42.720
Then make him wait two years for you!

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:48.240
B-But I need to find a job and I have a few things I'd like to do, too.

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:55.240
Not to mention he's always chasing after his baseball dream at full-speed,

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:59.060
so I don't know if he's even considering marriage with me.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.420
Hey.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.340
It's been a while, Goro.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.510
You've had a pretty rough season.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.850
Yeah, nothing new.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:16.720
With the World Cup, I was in a slump at the beginning of spring.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:20.020
It made me realize the difficulty of playing as a second-year.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.350
Yeah, right!

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.170
You still got the RBI title.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.650
That's because all the batters before me got on base.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.390
Is your sister well?

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:31.760
Oh, yeah.

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.770
We don't see each other much,

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:38.870
but we promised to live together when she gets accepted at a university in Tokyo.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.880
Really?

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.960
That's good.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:50.880
By the way, I heard Mayumura won the Sawamura Award for winning the most games and having the lowest ERA.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.310
Yeah.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:55.090
The Oceans placed fifth, so it definitely wasn't a fluke or anything.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:59.370
He got me out so many times that I didn't even want to see his face.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:03.460
I wonder if he'll come over some day...

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:04.770
to the majors.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.340
Toshi.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.520
How about you?

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.620
I just became a professional in Japan.

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:21.160
But when Japan starts to feel too small,

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:25.220
maybe it wouldn't be a bad idea to play against you in America.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.310
If I could, at the World Series.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.200
What?

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.470
You won't catch my pitches?

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.160
I'll do that after I beat you.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:48.020
Are you prepared to be the wife of a major leaguer?

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:52.150
A major leaguer's wife, huh?

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:58.600
I can't cook or speak English.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:01.340
I wonder if I could really do it.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.880
Sis, you've got some company.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.090
I'm home.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:14.000
Goro, Sophia said she's going back to America.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.030
Yeah, I heard she got permission from the management.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:21.090
At last, I can feel at home.

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:23.180
She asked for Shimizu's address,

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:24.510
but did something happen?

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:26.120
Wh-What?

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.110
Don't tell me she's up to something again!

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.190
Good evening.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:33.280
Sophia...

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:34.530
Why are you...

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:38.820
I wanted to apologize to you before I went back to America.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.880
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.180
Although Shigeno's working for us,

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.960
it wasn't my place to say those things.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.450
Besides, it looks like I was worried for nothing.

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:56.420
I talked with him on the way home last night.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.460
He was in a bad mood the whole way back.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:05.140
He was appalled at me for making you choose between breaking up and marriage when you're still in school.

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.190
So I asked him what his thoughts were,

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.610
and he gave me an answer on the spot.

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:19.740
I haven't put much thought into marriage or starting a family,

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:23.320
and I have no clue when it'll happen,

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:31.150
but if Shimizu decides she wouldn't mind spending the rest of her life with a baseball fanatic like me,

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:34.820
then I'll wait, no matter how long it takes.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:37.170
Be it ten or even twenty years.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.470
So I'm sure he won't push himself too hard for your sake.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.680
I'm leaving him in your care.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:48.940
I want to see him!

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.490
Finding a job...

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:55.880
Being unfit to be a major leaguer's wife because I can't cook or speak English...

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:59.320
All those things are so trivial!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.060
Oh?

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:04.290
Shimizu.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:05.700
Honda...

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.320
I see.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.650
So she went home after apologizing to you.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:12.540
Yeah.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.750
Well, that's the least she could have done.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:20.420
Who did she think she was, telling you to decide between marriage and breaking up?

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.260
Sorry, Honda.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:31.610
I hadn't thought about marriage at all until Sophia brought it up.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.480
Of course you hadn't.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.460
I hadn't either.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:37.150
That's not it!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:42.220
It's not because I'm still a student and I'm not ready.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.570
When I thought about marriage,

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:49.500
I found a side of me that didn't want to face the reality of being a major leaguer's wife.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:55.630
I mean, I was definitely not mentally prepared,

00:19:55.630 --> 00:20:00.350
and didn't know how you felt about me,

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:03.760
but while you felt that you wanted to spend the rest of your life with me,

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:08.180
I didn't have the strength to support you as soon as I could!

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.280
Geez.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.740
Who asked her to tell you what I said?

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.690
That's natural.

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:28.620
That's how it is.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:31.770
You can find a job after you graduate.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:33.870
It's your life.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.540
You don't have to pace yourself with me.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:43.070
Besides, you don't need to feel pressure about having to support Shigeno Goro, the major leaguer.

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:44.430
Walk at your own pace.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:49.810
When you feel you're ready to deal with a guy like me,

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:54.730
be my catcher for the rest of my life.

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:00.810
Yeah.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.370
<b>8 Years Later</b>

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:11.540
With three wins and three losses, this is the final game between the Hornets and the Raiders in the World Series.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:14.260
The game was tied at 7 after the eighth inning,

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:19.500
and the Hornets turn the mound over to their closer to reach for their first World Series title.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:24.630
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 56:

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:27.760
Goro Shigeno!

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:33.710
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:33.710
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:38.730
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:38.730
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:43.760
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:43.760
the only thing I truly have

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:48.090
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:48.090
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:56.440
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:56.440
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:21:56.440 --> 00:22:01.490
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:21:56.440 --> 00:22:01.490
the season of the coming summer began.

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:06.540
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:06.540
I had begun to understand many things

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:11.660
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:11.670
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:16.730
garakuta no yama kara

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:16.730
In the junk I've piled up,

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:21.150
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:21.150
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:26.070
hibike kono koe yo

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:26.070
Let my voice echo on.

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:32.330
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:32.330
Let my heart resonate.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:37.370
namida kareru made

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:37.370
Until my tears dry up,

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:42.670
tomo ni asu mita kimi yo mada

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:42.670
I need you to face the future we saw together.

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:47.250
namida hareru made

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:47.250
While my tears have yet to clear away,

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:52.550
warehito yukue sutekirenu nara

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:52.550
I just can't look away from my dream,

00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:56.270
egakikake no ima

00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:56.270
and I'll continue to paint the present,

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:03.270
omoide ni shinaide

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:03.270
so don't turn it into memories to reminisce about.

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:25.420
namida kareru made

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:25.420
Until my tears dry up,

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:30.380
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:30.380
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:35.010
namida hareru made

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:35.010
Until my tears clear away,

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:40.180
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:40.180
though I may lose my way,

00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:44.090
egakikake no ima

00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:44.090
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:51.090
kizamu akashi kono te de

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:51.090
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:59.250
Let's go, Toshi!

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.400
Ready when you are, Goro!

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:23.310
Daddy, let's play catch!

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:25.430
All right, I'm in!
